    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (80.06) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (78.50) serving as our primary offensive anchors. **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from a highly favorable matchup against Jameson Taillon, where his elite xwOBA (.421) and platoon advantage make him the most reliable play in the lineup despite a slight drag from wind conditions. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** presents the most fascinating upside play; while his #9 lineup spot is suboptimal, the combination of a high-xERA opponent (4.97) and a slow pitcher delivery creates an ideal environment for his elite speed to generate stolen base value\u2014the most critical scarcity we monitor. **Colt Keith** (69.64) and **Junior Caminero** (69.35) are our next strongest contributors, both benefiting significantly from top-of-the-order protections and park factors that lift their efficiency scores well into the \"Strong\" territory.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Caleb Durbin**, who narrowly missed the cut at 44.97. While **Caleb Durbin** typically carries high utility due to his profile, he was bypassed because of a difficult matchup against Connor Prielipp\u2019s low xERA (3.44) and a projected #9 batting position, which limits his counting stat upside compared to the starters. Conversely, **Casey Schmitt** (57.89) secured a spot over him by capitalizing on a favorable wind-out condition and a significant platoon edge against Davis Martin. We remain cautious regarding the reliance on \"Lineup Pending\" statuses for **Dillon Dingler**, **Luke Raley**, and others; if official lineups shift these players down the order or onto the pine, the efficiency scores will crater instantly. Special attention must be paid to **Christian Yelich** (43.92), whose score is tethered to the floor; he remains active only for his speed potential against Justin Wrobleski, but his current platoon disadvantage against the lefty makes him a high-risk candidate for a mid-game substitution if the Zebras need to prioritize AVG protection.",
